BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Understanding Social Security
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T131500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T141500
UID:69f6621dbd5c392c764807c5@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you understand how Social Security works? Have you wondered
  who is eligible for Social Security payments?\nThis engaging and educatio
 nal workshop\, presented by AARP\, focuses on building a basic understand
 ing of Social Security\, exploring how claiming decisions affect payments\
 , identifying useful resources\, and helping you build confidence in makin
 g the right decisions for your personal situation.
LOCATION:Aloha Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f6621dbd5c392c764807c5
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ready\, Set\, Kindergarten: Reading & Writing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T154500
UID:69ceb0b1129f1274383620aa@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready\, Set\, Kindergarten is a special 5-class series designe
 d for families. We will help you and your child get ready for Kindergarten
  with music\, stories\, art\, and play! All participants get a free book a
 t each class they attend. Ages 4-5.\nMay 26: Read to Learn\nMay 28: Let's
  Be Friends\nJune 2: Reading & Writing\nJune 4: Let's Talk\nJune 9: Playin
 g Together
LOCATION:Beaverton City Library\, Storytime Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ceb0b1129f1274383620aa
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All Ages Storytime Session 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T101500
UID:69b9c386b48451fc3c09987c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome preschoolers birth to six and their caregivers!\nAtten
 ding All Ages Storytime is a great way to build a caring bond between chil
 d and adult.\nIn this program\, you and your child will sing songs\, liste
 n to stories\, dance to music\, engage in interactive play\, and so much m
 ore!\n10 minutes of playtime follows session 1. 30 minutes of playtime fol
 lows session 2.\nArrive anytime between 9:30 a.m. – 10:00a.m. to enjoy t
 his program. We understand how difficult it is to be punctual with childre
 n. Playtime is just as beneficial as the storytime.\nThe library opens at 
 10:00 a.m.
LOCATION:Sherwood Public Library\, Community Room\, main floor
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b9c386b48451fc3c09987c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
