BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moth vs. Mantis Match-up
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260601T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260831T235959
UID:69fe7d2f1773192800187e73@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Spice up your Summer Reading with a little friendly competitio
 n! Visit the Teen Scene\, come to teen events\, scroll the library’s Ins
 tagram\, and explore the Fanno Creek Trail to find QR codes recruiting you
  for a team competition. Whenever you find a new QR code\, you can make an
 other entry. The team with the most entries gets to pick the theme for a f
 all celebration!
LOCATION:Tigard Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe7d2f1773192800187e73
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Letter Party with the Joy Mail Project
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T160000
UID:69fe7c8543b41b3d006535fa@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Plant a seed of connection and sow some joy! Write or decorate
  letters for seniors\, pediatric patients\, and other community members ex
 periencing isolation. This craft for a cause is presented in partnership w
 ith the Joy Mail Project\, an organization that aims to spread community p
 ositivity through creativity.
LOCATION:Tigard Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe7c8543b41b3d006535fa
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bee Amazed! with the UO Museum of Natural and Cultural History
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T163000
UID:69fe7c281773192800187e53@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Catch the buzz and zoom into the wonderful world of Oregon bee
 s! Did you know we have more than 500 kinds? Discover mason bees\, cuckoo 
 bees\, mining bees\, longhorn bees\, honeybees and more. Enjoy lots of han
 ds-on science fun and buzz-worthy activities while exploring these mighty 
 mini-beasts of nature.
LOCATION:Tigard Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe7c281773192800187e53
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Leap into Language & Literacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T160000
UID:69cc5ace8089f23c6765e5b9@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Language and literacy development is essential for children of
  all ages and backgrounds. Come and learn how to encourage language and li
 teracy development for the children in your program by focusing on the fiv
 e literacy practices (talking\, reading\, writing\, singing\, and playing)
  identified and adapted from the Every Child Ready to Read curriculum avai
 lable through your local library. Set One\; Core Knowledge Category: Human
  Growth & Development\; 2 hours\; Infant/Toddler\, Preschool\; Language: E
 nglish.\nRegistration required.
LOCATION:Beaverton City Library\, Meeting Room B
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cc5ace8089f23c6765e5b9
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
