BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Protect Our Trees
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T090000
UID:69fcfbd4f89ee15800514d7a@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Trees are an amazing resource: they clean the air and water\, 
 provide shade\, improve our mental health\, and so much more. The bigger t
 hey are\, the bigger their impact. Join\nTreekeepers of Washington County\
 nto learn about all the benefits of trees and what you can do to make sure
  that our big trees stick around for future generations. They will also sh
 owcase some notable trees in Cedar Mill.
LOCATION:Cedar Mill Library\, Elm & Oak Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fcfbd4f89ee15800514d7a
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
