BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lee's Association Lion Dance Team
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T114500
UID:69d97c09bd9a3c316a522b34@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:It is the Year of the Fire Horse and Lee's Association Lion Da
 nce Team will be making an appearance at our summer reading lineup.\nFesti
 ve\, expressive\, engaging for all ages\, and these are just a few words t
 hat describe this cultural event.\nThis is an outdoor venue. We will have 
 some shade/rain tents\, but attendees are encouraged to dress for the weat
 her.\nThe Sherwood YMCA will be providing free lunches to all families who
  attend. Thank you YMCA!\nA very special Thank You to Stan and Diana Stanl
 ey. This program is extra-special for us today not only because it is spon
 sored by them\, but it is also in honor of their daughter Theresa Kaishin 
 Stanley. Theresa was a volunteer at our library and will always be part of
  our library family. Her cheerful energy and smile always brought us so mu
 ch joy...and we truly hope that today's performance brings you all a littl
 e bit of that joy as well.\nEveryone welcome!
LOCATION:Sherwood Public Library\, Cannery Square. 22622 SW Pine St. Sherw
 ood\, OR 97140
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d97c09bd9a3c316a522b34
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
