SUMMARY:Toddler Fun | Diversión para chiquitos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T103000
UID:6998db44b0595799c09e481b@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all toddlers (ages 1-3)! Get ready to test out your gr
 oss motor skills at the library. Crawl through tunnels\, jump over things\
 , and dance your wiggles away!\nNiños entre las edades de 1 y 3 años pre
 párense para poner a prueba sus habilidades motores gruesas en la bibliot
 eca. Gatea a través del túnel\, salta por encima de los obstáculos\, ¡
 y baila hasta no poder más!
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6998db44b0595799c09e481b
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Book Discussion: The Women by Kristin Hannah
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T190000
UID:697bbfacb0595799c0996d3c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Read. Be inspired. Discuss.\nWe're hosting a book discussion i
 n person at the library. If you love to talk about the books you've read\
 , join us for a lively discussion of\nThe Women by Kristin Hannah\n\, wh
 ich may be available as an e-book and audiobook in Libby as well as physic
 al library copies which can be checked out. The first 10 people to regist
 er for this program can be given copies of the book provided generously by
  Friends of Sherwood Public Library.\nRegistration online is encouraged bu
 t not required.\nFrom the publisher:\nWomen can be heroes. When twenty-yea
 r-old nursing student Frances "Frankie" McGrath hears these unexpected wor
 ds\, it is a revelation. Raised on idyllic Coronado Island and sheltered b
 y her conservative parents\, she has always prided herself on doing the ri
 ght thing\, being a good girl. But in 1965 the world is changing\, and she
  suddenly imagines a different choice for her life. When her brother ships
  out to serve in Vietnam\, she impulsively joins the Army Nurse Corps and 
 follows his path. As green and inexperienced as the men sent to Vietnam to
  fight\, Frankie is overwhelmed by the chaos and destruction of war\, as w
 ell as the unexpected trauma of coming home to a changed and politically d
 ivided America.
LOCATION:Sherwood Public Library\, Community Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697bbfacb0595799c0996d3c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Read to the Dogs/Lee a los perros
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T163000
UID:6932400b94297d36009e5b18@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to build your skills and confidence? Read aloud to a trai
 ned therapy dog (accompanied by their handler) in a private 20-minute sess
 ion. Grades K – 12.\n¿Quieres mejorar tus habilidades y tu confianza? I
 nscríbete para leer en voz alta a perros de terapia (acompañados por un 
 entrenador) en una sesión privada de 20 minutos. K – 12o grado.\nYou ma
 y sign up for one(1) Read to the Dogs session within a one(1) month period
 .
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6932400b94297d36009e5b18
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shameless Romance Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T193000
UID:69fbbc02278f7c2f008b8ef0@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Our Shameless Romance Book Club’s next read is\nThe Prospect
 s\nby KT Hoffman!\nAs the first openly transgender player in professional 
 baseball\, Gene\n Ionescu is just happy to have a career playing the sport
  he loves. \nWhile no one’s idea of a major league prospect\, he loves h
 is spot on his\n minor league team\, the Beaverton Beavers. Gene has every
 thing he’s \nhoped for\, until his college rival Luis Estrada is traded 
 to the Beavers\n and takes Gene’s position. As the two begrudgingly lear
 n to work \ntogether on the field\, they realize they may have more than j
 ust a love \nof baseball in common. Will Gene strike out at his chance at 
 happiness\, \nor will Luis teach him how to swing for the fences?\nReserve
  a copy here\n. Also available in eBook and downloadable audiobook formats
 .\nThis will be the last SRBC meeting before we take a summer break! \nThe
 re will be no book club meetings in July or August. We will return on\n Tu
 esday\, September 8th.\nWant to read ahead?\nCheck out the Shameless Roman
 ce Book Club’s schedule and titles for the rest of 2026!
LOCATION:Aloha Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fbbc02278f7c2f008b8ef0
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Navigator One on One Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T120000
UID:69826f761e64afd01e58efcc@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Digital Navigator One-On-One Tech Help each Wednesday from 10:
 00 a.m. -12:00 p.m. in the library. Need help with digital questions or jo
 b searches? This free program is in partnership with American Connection C
 orps & The Washington County Cooperative Library Services. Call the librar
 y at 503 324-1382 to schedule a session.\nIf no appointments are scheduled
  drop in tech help will be available.\nThe Digital Navigator Program (DNP)
  is a free service made possible by a partnership\nbetween Washington Coun
 ty Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the Washington\nCounty Broadba
 nd Action Team. The DNP is funded in part by American Connections\nCorps\,
  an AmeriCorps program dedicated to advancing economic prosperity by bridg
 ing\nthe digital divide. This project is being supported\, in part\, by fe
 deral award number\nSLFRP0228 awarded to Washington County by the U.S. Dep
 artment of the Treasury.
LOCATION:Banks Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69826f761e64afd01e58efcc
