BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Navigator One on One Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260708T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260708T120000
UID:69826f761e64afd01e58efcb@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Digital Navigator One-On-One Tech Help each Wednesday from 10:
 00 a.m. -12:00 p.m. in the library. Need help with digital questions or jo
 b searches? This free program is in partnership with American Connection C
 orps & The Washington County Cooperative Library Services. Call the librar
 y at 503 324-1382 to schedule a session.\nIf no appointments are scheduled
  drop in tech help will be available.\nThe Digital Navigator Program (DNP)
  is a free service made possible by a partnership\nbetween Washington Coun
 ty Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the Washington\nCounty Broadba
 nd Action Team. The DNP is funded in part by American Connections\nCorps\,
  an AmeriCorps program dedicated to advancing economic prosperity by bridg
 ing\nthe digital divide. This project is being supported\, in part\, by fe
 deral award number\nSLFRP0228 awarded to Washington County by the U.S. Dep
 artment of the Treasury.
LOCATION:Banks Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69826f761e64afd01e58efcb
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plant a Seed | Planta una semilla
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T170000
UID:69e2e736defec6489cbe935c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This year's Summer Reading Challenge theme is\, "Plant a Seed"
  and that's exactly what we're going to do for our first summer program! L
 earn all about germination and how tiny seeds become extraordinary plants 
 with some hands-on learning. Plant sunflower seeds\, build greenhouses\, a
 nd examine plants up close with microscopes from their flowers to their ro
 ots. Fun for all ages!\nEl tema del Reto de Lectura de Verano de este año
  es "Planta una semilla"\, ¡y eso es precisamente lo que haremos en nuest
 ro primer programa de verano! Aprende todo sobre la germinación y cómo l
 as diminutas semillas se convierten en plantas extraordinarias con activid
 ades prácticas. Planta semillas de girasol\, construye invernaderos y exa
 mina las plantas de cerca con microscopios\, desde sus flores hasta sus ra
 íces. ¡Diversión para todas las edades!
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e2e736defec6489cbe935c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One Book\, One Coast Watch Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T150000
UID:69e69f27defec6489cbf2180@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Aloha Community Library is joining more than 130 library s
 ystems \non the West Coast for a shared community reading experience! Libr
 ary \nusers at all participating locations are invited to read the graphic
  \nmemoir\nThey Called Us Enemy\n\, recounting actor\, author\, and \nacti
 vist George Takei’s childhood imprisonment within American \nincarcerati
 on camps during World War II.\nRequest your copy on hold from our catalog\
 n\, or\naccess the e-book version on Libby\nimmediately – unlimited digi
 tal copies will be available through Saturday 6/6!\nFinished reading and r
 eady to discuss?\nFind discussion opportunities\nat various WCCLS librarie
 s!\nOne Book\, One Coast will close with a special author talk hosted on \
 nSunday 5/31 at the East Los Angeles Library and featuring George Takei. \
 nGeorge will discuss the experiences that led to the creation of his \nmem
 oir\, what it means to be a good neighbor and citizen in the face of \nove
 rwhelming challenges\, and how shared books and stories build stronger\n c
 ommunities.\nRegister to watch the livestream online\n\, or join us here a
 t the Aloha Community Library for a watch party! Our doors will open at 1:
 45pm.
LOCATION:Aloha Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e69f27defec6489cbf2180
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bike Repair and Safety Workshop with WashCo Bikes  | Taller de rep
 aración y seguridad en bicicletas con WashCo Bikes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T150000
UID:6a0a5402a99bdd027d420aef@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to learn how to adjust\, clean\, and repair your bicycle 
 in a friendly\, encouraging and instructive atmosphere? Bring your bike to
  our Bike Repair Clinic\, and WashCo Bikes’ qualified instructors will t
 each you how to maintain and fix it! As an added bonus\, WashCo Bikes will
  also cover Bike Safety - using hand signals\, helmet fitting and general 
 traffic safety. For teens and adults. Provided in English and Spanish.\n¿
 Quiere aprender a ajustar\, limpiar y reparar su bicicleta en un ámbito a
 bierto\, animado e instructivo? ¡Trae su bicicleta a una clínica para la
  reparación de bicicletas! Instructores de WashCo Bikes les ensenará a r
 ealizar el mantenimiento básico de las bicis. Adicionalmente\, en el tall
 er de seguridad en bicicleta\, aprenda a hacer señales con las manos\, el
 egir un casco adecuado y circular correctamente cuando hay coches cerca. E
 n ingles y español. Para adolesentes y adultos.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Shute Park
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0a5402a99bdd027d420aef
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Navigator 1:1 Tech Help with Brian
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T131500
UID:69fbc3a55a8c322f03c750cb@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get a one-on-one appointment with a friendly\, knowledgeable D
 igital Navigator who will help you find answers to your questions about yo
 ur mobile devices\, personal computer\, websites\, getting started with te
 ch\, and more! Bring your device or use a library \ncomputer.\nOnce you re
 gister a staff member will contact you for additional details.\nThe Digita
 l Navigator Program (DNP) is a free service made possible \nby a partnersh
 ip between Washington County Cooperative Library Services \n(WCCLS) and th
 e American Connection Corps\, who empowers its members and\n the communiti
 es they serve to address digital disparities and create \nlasting change.
LOCATION:West Slope Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fbc3a55a8c322f03c750cb
