BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall prevention\, balance\, and healthy living
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T120000
UID:6a08b4488360de907d877370@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Falls are the leading cause of injury and death among Oregonia
 ns age 65 and older.\nThe  goal of this free workshop is to provide older 
 adults information and tools to help prevent a fall and to encourage livin
 g an active and healthy life. Topics covered include concussions and brain
  health\, medication interactions\, common reasons for falling\, home safe
 ty\, exercise\, and easy steps you can take to prevent a fall.\nIt covers 
 transportation and pedestrian related issues\, and we walk through a coupl
 e of the balance exercises.\nFree fall prevention items will be provided t
 o participants.\nRegistration is required. We need a minimum of 8 people r
 egistered to host this event.
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a08b4488360de907d877370
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
