BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One Book One Coast: Livestreamed Author Talk with George Takei
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T160000
UID:69b5f936403a4e5652df3318@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the largest book club on the West Coast!\nWest Slo
 pe Community Library will be hosting a viewing of the Author Talk with G
 eorge Takei\, livestreamed from Los Angeles.\nOne Book\, One Coast\nis a c
 ollaborative program uniting a wide network of West Coast libraries in a s
 hared celebration of literacy\, learning\, community\, and civil discourse
 . From April 1 through May 31st\, all participating libraries will read an
 d discuss\nThey Called Us Enemy\nby George Takei.\nThe largest book club o
 n the West Coast wraps up with a special visit from George Takei\, author 
 of They Called Us Enemy. We'll be talking to George about the experiences 
 that led to the creation of his memoir\, what it means to be a good neighb
 or and citizen in the face of overwhelming challenges\, and how shared boo
 ks and stories build stronger communities.\nGeorge Takei is a renowned civ
 il rights activist\, social media icon\, Grammy-nominated recording artist
 \, New York Times bestselling author\, and pioneering actor whose career h
 as spanned over six decades. Best known for his role as Hikaru Sulu in Sta
 r Trek\, Takei has appeared in more than 40 feature films and hundreds of 
 television episodes. He has leveraged his public profile to champion socia
 l justice\, LGBTQ+ rights\, and marriage equality.\nTakei’s advocacy is 
 deeply personal. As a child during World War II\, he and his family were a
 mong the 125\,000 Japanese Americans unjustly imprisoned in U.S. incarcera
 tion camps—a formative experience that shaped his lifelong commitment to
  civil rights and public service.\nThey Called Us Enemy\nis a graphic memo
 ir recounting actor/author/activist George Takei’s childhood imprisoned 
 within American concentration camps during World War II. Confronting quest
 ions of patriotism\, family\, loyalty\, and community\, George’s work is
  a stunning examination of what it means to be American\, both then and no
 w.\nRead "They Called Us Enemy" at WCCLS\nIf you'd like to watch the Autho
 r Talk from home- you can\nregister here.\nNote: the library\nis\nclosed o
 n Sunday\, but will open just for this event between 2 and 4.
LOCATION:West Slope Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b5f936403a4e5652df3318
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Atelier: Charcoal Drawing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T193000
UID:69f2686766c3387a9d0851f1@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bring a friend and join us Wednesday nights for an art worksho
 p! Enjoy dedicated time for art and unwinding. In the month of June we wil
 l host two classes exploring drawing with charcoal. We will use a differen
 t beginner-friendly still life in each class. During the sessions we will 
 draft simplified shapes and use charcoal to block in values\, with a focus
  on constructive corrections\, adding highlights and detail. All materials
  are provided and all skill levels are welcome.\nFor adults and teens 14+.
  Registration is required. Held in the Makerspace.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f2686766c3387a9d0851f1
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flower Painting | Pintura de flores
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T170000
UID:69fa92a943b41b3d006473d7@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Before synthetic materials\, we used to get our paints\, dyes\
 , and inks from natural sources including flowers. Let's relearn how to e
 xtract and process natural inks from differently colored flowers\, then u
 se them to recolor plain petals to create our own beautiful designs!\nThi
 s program is for all ages.\nAntes de la llegada de los materiales sintéti
 cos\, obteníamos nuestras pinturas\, tintes y tintas de fuentes naturales
 \, como las flores. ¡Reaprendamos a extraer y procesar tintas naturales d
 e flores de diferentes colores y luego usémoslas para teñir pétalos y c
 rear nuestros propios diseños!\nEste programa es para todas las edades.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa92a943b41b3d006473d7
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tortilla Tutorial | Tutorial de Tortilla
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T170000
UID:69fa9277e8af4a2f00707e9a@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:There's nothing quite like farm to table food\, especially whe
 n making traditional\, seasonal dishes. Learn how to make authentic corn 
 tortillas with a simple yet delicious recipe that can be easily replicated
  at home for you to enjoy again and again!\nThis event is for adults.\nNo 
 hay nada como la comida de la granja a la mesa\, especialmente al preparar
  platos tradicionales de temporada. Aprende a hacer tortillas de maíz aut
 énticas con una receta sencilla pero deliciosa que podrás replicar fáci
 lmente en casa para disfrutarlas una y otra vez.\nEste evento es para adul
 tos.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa9277e8af4a2f00707e9a
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Andy Zamenes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T170000
UID:69fa923943b41b3d006473d2@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:See award-winning children’s performer and songwriter\, Andy
  Z\, who blends music\, movement\, storytelling\, and puppetry into an int
 eractive experience that delights kids and entertains the whole family.\nA
 ndy Zamenes\, is a multiple award-winning singer\, songwriter\, arranger\,
  scriptwriter\, and voting member of NARAS (Grammy® Awards) from the San 
 Francisco Bay Area. Andy's music has been heard on NBC's Today Show and hi
 s music and performances have been featured in the Pandora Video Series an
 d on the Pottery Barn Kids Stylehouse website.\nDescubre a Andy Z\, galard
 onado artista y compositor infantil\, que combina música\, movimiento\, n
 arración y títeres en una experiencia interactiva que deleita a los niñ
 os y entretiene a toda la familia.\nAndy Zamenes es un cantante\, composit
 or\, arreglista y guionista multipremiado\, además de miembro votante de 
 NARAS (Premios Grammy®) originario del Área de la Bahía de San Francisc
 o. Su música se ha escuchado en el programa Today Show de NBC y sus actua
 ciones han aparecido en la serie de videos de Pandora y en el sitio web St
 ylehouse de Pottery Barn Kids.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa923943b41b3d006473d2
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature in Resin | Naturaleza en Resina
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260710T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260710T190000
UID:69fa923543b41b3d006473d0@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Resin is a natural preservative that has been valued by humans
  since prehistory both for its innate beauty\, and for the flora and fauna
  that sometimes becomes caught in it\, remaining perfectly intact for eons
 . Now we'll make our own resin art preserving natural flora in resin and t
 urning them into bookmarks\, coasters\, rings\, and other fun trinkets!\nT
 his program is for teens aged 13-18.\nLa resina es un conservante natural 
 que la humanidad ha valorado desde la prehistoria tanto por su belleza int
 rínseca como por la flora y fauna que a veces queda atrapada en ella\, pe
 rmaneciendo perfectamente intactas durante eones. ¡Ahora crearemos nuestr
 o propio arte con resina\, conservando flora natural y transformándola en
  marcapáginas\, posavasos\, anillos y otros divertidos objetos!\nEste pro
 grama está dirigido a adolescentes de 13 a 18 años.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa923543b41b3d006473d0
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Amazing Bubble Man | El asombroso hombre burbuja
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T170000
UID:69fa922443b41b3d006473cc@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Amazing Bubble Man\, Louis Pearl\, is floating over to the
  library to put on his iconic bubble show! In a show combining art\, scien
 ce\, and plenty of spectacle\, he'll show us things you wouldn't think pos
 sible with a bit of soap and some bubble wands! From rainbow bubbles\, to 
 people inside bubbles\, to bubbles the size of elephants and more\, you wo
 n't want to miss this exciting show!\nThis program is for all ages.\n¡El 
 asombroso hombre burbuja\, Louis Pearl\, llega a la biblioteca para presen
 tar su icónico espectáculo de burbujas! En un show que combina arte\, ci
 encia y mucha magia\, nos mostrará cosas que no creerías posibles con un
  poco de jabón y varitas de burbujas. Desde burbujas arcoíris hasta pers
 onas dentro de burbujas\, pasando por burbujas del tamaño de elefantes y 
 mucho más\, ¡no querrás perderte este emocionante espectáculo!\nEste p
 rograma es para todas las edades.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa922443b41b3d006473cc
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thinking About AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260629T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260629T143000
UID:6a10905b490f176f7dd60dc3@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI is turning up everywhere we look these days\, and there is 
 a lot to think about! In this program\, we’ll cover basic AI terminology
  and look at how it works. We'll review examples of How AI is used today\,
  as well as how it might be used in the future. We’ll\n also discuss the
  risks and concerns that we all need to consider when \nthinking about how
  to interact with AI in our lives. AI may be changing \nthe world\; what k
 ind of world do we want it to become?\nThis Library program will be held i
 n the Vista Room at Courtyard Village Raleigh Hills and is open to the gen
 eral public.\nRegistration is optional. If you register with your email ad
 dress\, you can receive the presentation materials and additional resource
 s after the program.
LOCATION:West Slope Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a10905b490f176f7dd60dc3
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dungeon Mastery 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T160000
UID:69ff5ab8055b429f3b3ab8dd@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This Summer level up your Dungeons & Dragons game by becoming 
 a Dungeon Master! Every D&D game needs one player to take charge and creat
 e a world full of quests\, monsters\, treasure and adventure\; maybe you
 ’d like to BE that player… Learn the basics of D&D and how to run your
  own campaign for your friends with an experienced DM. We’ll discuss bas
 ic principles of running a game\, how to run a session 0 to lay the ground
 work\, creating a party of adventurers\, how to prep for a session- and wh
 at to do when your players run in a completely different direction than yo
 u expected!\nNo prior experience is needed- whether you’ve never played 
 before and want to learn how to start your own game\, or you’re a player
  who wants to try being a Dungeon Master\, or even if you’ve done some D
 Ming and just want to sharpen your skills with input from new players\, al
 l are welcome. This program will cover 5-6 sessions over the Summer (depen
 ding on the number of participants) to give everyone a chance to run an ad
 venture for the others and experience Dungeon Mastery from behind the DM s
 creen.\nSpace is necessarily limited\, so registration is required.This pr
 ogram is intended for teens ages 13-17.
LOCATION:West Slope Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ff5ab8055b429f3b3ab8dd
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yarn Craft Club | Club de manualidades con hilo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T150000
UID:69ceca20f29b90618efd36fc@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun and creative gathering at our knitting\, cro
 cheting\, and stitching meet-up! Everyone is welcome\, regardless of skill
  level—whether you’re a seasoned pro or just starting out. Feel free t
 o bring your own project to work on\, or come and learn something new\; we
 ’re here to help you get started.\nThis program is open to all ages.\n¡
 Únete a nosotros para una reunión divertida y creativa en nuestro encuen
 tro de tejido\, crochet y costura! Todos son bienvenidos\, sin importar su
  nivel\, ya seas un profesional experimentado o estés empezando. Siéntet
 e libre de traer tu propio proyecto o venir a aprender algo nuevo\; estamo
 s aquí para ayudarte a empezar.\nEste programa es para todas las edades.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ceca20f29b90618efd36fc
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
