DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T120000
UID:69826f761e64afd01e58efca@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Digital Navigator One-On-One Tech Help each Wednesday from 10:
 00 a.m. -12:00 p.m. in the library. Need help with digital questions or jo
 b searches? This free program is in partnership with American Connection C
 orps & The Washington County Cooperative Library Services. Call the librar
 y at 503 324-1382 to schedule a session.\nIf no appointments are scheduled
  drop in tech help will be available.\nThe Digital Navigator Program (DNP)
  is a free service made possible by a partnership\nbetween Washington Coun
 ty Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the Washington\nCounty Broadba
 nd Action Team. The DNP is funded in part by American Connections\nCorps\,
  an AmeriCorps program dedicated to advancing economic prosperity by bridg
 ing\nthe digital divide. This project is being supported\, in part\, by fe
 deral award number\nSLFRP0228 awarded to Washington County by the U.S. Dep
 artment of the Treasury.
LOCATION:Banks Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69826f761e64afd01e58efca
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Power of Place: An Exhibit for Oregon 250
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T235959
UID:69fd019a1773192800183415@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Immerse yourself in the breathtaking beauty of Oregon through 
 The Power of Place\, a digital exhibition featuring photographs by acclaim
 ed photographer Peter Marbach that celebrate the state’s diverse landsca
 pes. From the rugged coastline and towering mountains to the serene High D
 esert and other cherished landmarks\, this collection invites you to explo
 re the places that continue to inspire and connect us all.\nThis exhibit w
 ill be up in at Cedar Mill and Bethany Libraries with images spending tim
 e at each location. Brought to us in partnership with the Oregon Historica
 l Society and the\nAmerica 250 Oregon Commission\n.
LOCATION:Bethany Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fd019a1773192800183415
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
