BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bike Repair and Safety Workshop with WashCo Bikes | Taller de repa
 ración y seguridad en bicicletas con WashCo Bikes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T160000
UID:6a0a347a748daf857d58f606@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to learn how to adjust\, clean\, and repair your bicycle 
 in a friendly\, encouraging and instructive atmosphere? Bring your bike to
  our Bike Repair Clinic\, and WashCo Bikes’ qualified instructors will t
 each you how to maintain and fix it! As an added bonus\, WashCo Bikes will
  also cover Bike Safety - using hand signals\, helmet fitting and general 
 traffic safety. For teens and adults. Provided in English and Spanish.\n¿
 Quiere aprender a ajustar\, limpiar y reparar su bicicleta en un ámbito a
 bierto\, animado e instructivo? ¡Trae su bicicleta a una clínica para la
  reparación de bicicletas! Instructores de WashCo Bikes les ensenará a r
 ealizar el mantenimiento básico de las bicis. Adicionalmente\, en el tall
 er de seguridad en bicicleta\, aprenda a hacer señales con las manos\, el
 egir un casco adecuado y circular correctamente cuando hay coches cerca. E
 n ingles y español. Para adolesentes y adultos.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0a347a748daf857d58f606
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CivicUs: What Does It Mean to Be a Citizen?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T153000
UID:69fe5873c7d3cd580057f95c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In the United States\, most people would say they believe in d
 emocracy. But do we all understand the word in the same way? Where does th
 e concept of democracy come from\, and what makes “the rule of the peopl
 e” work? This conversation will dig into the history\, philosophy\, and 
 practical workings of democracy. We’ll look at the words of important po
 litical thinkers from the past\, the US Constitution\, and research on cha
 llenges to democracy in the present day. We’ll leave with a better sense
  of what we mean when we say democracy and how to participate in the democ
 ratic process locally and nationally.\nFacilitator Prakash Chenjeri is a p
 rofessor and chair of the philosophy program at Southern Oregon University
 . He was educated both in India and the US. His research and teaching focu
 s on understanding the concept of citizenship\, the role of scientific lit
 eracy in modern democracy\, and debates over science and religion. He co-d
 irects the Democracy Project\, a comprehensive examination of democracy ar
 ound the world in the twenty-first century. He has lived in Oregon for mor
 e than three decades.\nThis program is part of Oregon Humanities’ Consid
 er This: Beyond 250 conversation series.\nRegistration required.
LOCATION:Beaverton City Library\, Meeting Room B
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe5873c7d3cd580057f95c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
