BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Belong! Employing Visual Supports to Teach Children With Autism
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T120000
UID:688be1c7d234473d0028a736@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Visual supports mean using a picture or other visual item to c
 ommunicate with a child who has difficulty understanding or using language
 .  In this class participants will explore a variety of visual tools to us
 e for children with autism\, look at when it’s helpful\, how to teach an
 d use it and what to do when challenging behaviors arise.\nCKC - SN\, 1.5 
 LEC\, 1.5 SN | 3 hours | Set Two | ARC: IT & PS\nTrainer: Kelley Lawson\nT
 his childcare provider training is hosted by Cedar Mill & Bethany Communi
 ty Libraries.
