BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Navigator Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T154500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T161500
UID:69c85287e2a2952aed0b4b16@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you need one-on-one assistance with your digital questions?
  A trusted guide can help you learn about home connectivity\, devices\, an
 d digital skills. Register for a slot. Bring your device or use a library 
 computer.\nRegistrants will be contacted for more details.\nSlots are 30-4
 0 minutes long. Sign up for your preferred time slot: 3\, 3:45\, 4:30\, or
  5:15. [We do not have a waitlist\; please call or visit the library the 
 day off the Digital Navigator appointment to check availability.]\nThe Dig
 ital Navigator Program (DNP) is a free service made possible by a partners
 hip between Washington County Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the
  American Connections Corps\, who empowers its members and the communities
  they serve to address digital disparities and create lasting change.
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, Enter via the rec center's main e
 ntrance and walk through the building to the library. Or use the doorbell 
 at the door by the library.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c85287e2a2952aed0b4b16
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bricks for Better Brains Monthly Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T160000
UID:69c85305b6c4ac1fedc8cf73@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bricks for Better Brains© encourages older people to explore 
 creativity\, strengthen social connections\, and take advantage of tactile
  stimulation.\nParticipants will work on a set or free build. All material
 s will be provided.\nAbout our presenter and the founder of Bricks for Bet
 ter Brains: Natalia Kasperovich is a university-educated chemical engineer
 \, community volunteer\, educator\, and most importantly\, a lifelong lear
 ner. She has an Associate Degree in Gerontology from Portland Community C
 ollege. She is a passionate advocate for continuous and self-motivated lea
 rning\, intergenerational understanding\, diversity\, and inclusivity.\nRe
 gistration is encouraged\; but not required. {It helps us know how many su
 pplies and how many tables and chairs to have set up beforehand.}
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, This event takes place in the lib
 rary's event room\, which is located next to the rec center's locker rooms
 .
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c85305b6c4ac1fedc8cf73
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Take & Make Craft: Koinobori Wind Socks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T235959
UID:69ea51de66c3387a9d07af7a@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:“Koinobori\n\, or carp streamers\, are a beloved symbol of C
 hildren’s Day in Japan\, celebrated annually on May 5th. These colorful 
 windsocks in the shape of carp are traditionally flown outside homes\, sch
 ools\, and public spaces to wish children strength\, health\, and success.
  The koinobori are designed to flutter and swim in the wind\, resembling c
 arp swimming upstream\, a metaphor for perseverance and growth.”\nhttps:
 //travel.rakuten.com/contents/usa/en-us/guide/koinobori/\nKit includes:\nP
 recut koinobori windsock\n2 washable markers\nCardstock strip\nLength of s
 tring for hanging\nYou provide:\nGlue\nScissors or hole punch\nMore marker
 s\, watercolor paints\, or whatever arts & crafts supplies you choose to a
 dd!\nRegister\nto reserve your kit and pick it up at West Slope Library at
  your convenience any time from May1st-31st* during the library's open hou
 rs. Some kits will also be available for pick up at the library\, no reser
 vation required.\nThese kits are graciously sponsored by the Cultural Coal
 ition of Washington County and the Oregon Cultural Trust.\nPlease limit 1
  kit per person\n.\nWe can't wait to see what you create! Send your pictur
 e by email to\nwestslope@wccls.org\nor tag us on Instagram @gardenhomecomm
 unitylibrary\n*Reserved kits not picked up by May 31st will be offered to
  those on the waitlist or first come\, first serve at the library.
LOCATION:West Slope Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ea51de66c3387a9d07af7a
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
