BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One Book\, One Coast
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T151500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T163000
UID:6a0e2228c6a1dc3d00d506c1@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a a library program uniting a network of West Coas
 t Libraries in a shared celebration of literacy\, learning\, community and
  civil discourse.\nThe chosen title is "They Called Us Enemy" by George Ta
 kei.  We will kick off this program by exploring the traditional Japanese
  method of fish printing called Gyotaku (don't worry\, we're not using rea
 l fish!).  We will have a few copies of the book to handout at the art ev
 ent.  Later\, we will discuss the book and attend a live-stream author ta
 lk.\nThursday April 16: Gyotaku fish printing and book handout\nTeen group
  3:15-4:30pm\nAdult group 6:30-8:00pm\nThursday May 28: Book Discussion\nT
 een group 3:15-4:30pm\nAdult group 6:30-8:00pm\nSunday May 31:  Live-Stre
 am Author Talk with George Takei\n2-4pm
LOCATION:Banks Public Library\, Jane Moore Community Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0e2228c6a1dc3d00d506c1
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
